{"title":"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Playing_with_the_answers)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Playing with the answers)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Note)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Note)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pyramid with a square base is cut by a plane that is parallel to its base and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units from the base. The surface area of the smaller pyramid that is cut from the top is half the surface area of the original pyramid. What is the altitude of the original pyramid?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/23843bbb375e927d74a4fd3b13cd2126fae32ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 2+\\sqrt{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 1+2\\sqrt{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 4+2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"511\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the two pyramids are similar, the ratio of the altitudes is the square root of the ratio of the surface areas.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the altitude of the larger pyramid, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c1dd3bbde066f5334db006cebf1c06cbe03807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-2$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> is the altitude of the smaller pyramid.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d250ff8d0d8bbdfbcd56aec44462e7f7b8759fdf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{a-2}=\\sqrt{\\frac21}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{1} \\longrightarrow a= a\\sqrt{2} - 2\\sqrt{2} \\longrightarrow a\\sqrt{2}-a=2\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/260de0f48842dd937c62036718b0fe7aeea25aa1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}-1} = \\frac{4+2\\sqrt{2}}{2-1} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) \\ } 4+2\\sqrt{2}}.\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Playing_with_the_answers.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Playing_with_the_answers)\">Solution 2 (Playing with the answers)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Playing with the answers)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Instead of actually solving this problem, we can play with the answers. The ratios of the altitudes squared is the ratio of the surface areas, so the answer choice has to be larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because an original height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> would give the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e0586d3649c943f13be520ee129b508ec68a3b88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> for the surface area and only choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Note.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Note)\">Solution 3 (Note)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Note)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in Solution 1, we used the fact that the ratio of surface area is the ratio of side lengths <i>squared</i>. However, with this, we can go two ways. \n</p><p>1. (Solution 1) The ratio of the surface area of the large pyramid to the surface area of the small pyramid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f4b3ad03256df73c0ec2b5ddecbc6b44eaad8ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so the ratio of their altitudes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5ebc27071fbe73a1a180f4551c9e9cc4513bbd4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac21}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{1}=\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"134\" height=\"45\" />. \n</p><p>2. (Another way) The ratio of the surface area of the small pyramid to the surface area of the large pyramid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dcd5e6a7667f87063bc60523fe5945cd667a2be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so the ratio of their altitudes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40cea3f2062cd1801b45439186c492311a3dce76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac12}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"138\" height=\"48\" />.  \n</p><p><br />\nThen, we can set up variables based on these ratios and solve for the variable, hence getting the altitude of the large triangle, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f311a4fcebea008cab4bf850f257471385fc4348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}~4+2\\sqrt 2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"116\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>~BakedPotato66\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ratio of the surface area of the smaller pyramid to the surface area of the larger pyramid is the same as the ratio of the area of the square face of the smaller pyramid to that of the larger pyramid. We take the cross-section through the apex of the larger pyramid, revealing a triangle with a line segment parallel to its base passing through it. Suppose the triangle has height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> (the original pyramid has altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />) and base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> (the original pyramid's square base has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />). Suppose further that the length of the line segment going through the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6c5ddfd368673c178f3323ce2994cdbc8fbdab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> (the smaller pyramid's square base has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6c5ddfd368673c178f3323ce2994cdbc8fbdab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />). By similar triangles, we have the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e0648403c35010ca76e6e1bdf300470b2121b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{h} = \\frac{s_2}{h-2} \\implies  s_2 = \\frac{s(h-2)}{h}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"244\" height=\"42\" />. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9c3126ac2585b5b06a762ec127a4f3c677fc4dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_2^2 = \\frac{1}{2}s^2 \\implies (\\frac{s(h-2)}{h})^2 = \\frac{1}{2}s^2 \\implies (h-2)^2 = \\frac{1}{2}h^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"432\" height=\"40\" />. Solving this equation, we get the solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d2947859dd32d7d331b5042ea93b6cff8785e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 4 + 2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24ec48ca4cbed2dc106fbc4179564c48d66425e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 4 - 2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"21\" />. However, with the second solution, the smaller pyramid would have a height that is two less than this, which would result in a negative number (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdf85c160748d8a1a8ccc827a67633500c4571b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 - 2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />). Thus, we discard the second solution, and our only solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577c4e580c56d4434ae7be5bfb357820e323c49c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}~4 + 2\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"111\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cxsmi\">cxsmi</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We find the volume ratio of the smaller pyramid to the bigger pyramid to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a04e1548b59dc64f3e7bbd82b9e5bb1e93bdacc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"39\" height=\"43\" />. Let the side length of the base of the smaller pyramid be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and the side length of the larger one be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/73547d212805cf6fd2b6c461e1c9e8d5c3761ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />. We can call the height of the smaller pyramid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and the larger pyramid's height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a98e21948e864385c38fc193895ae344bbc60f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We now set up a proportion and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f888c68ef1e08a72f3bafcb472bbfef4a3ec9e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}x^2 h}{\\frac{1}{3}(x\\sqrt{2})^2 (h+2)^2} = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"49\" />\nWe solve this proportion for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and add two at the end to get the height of the original pyramid to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/8/1e8b426539dabe92d4fe1ea5fa9616fbc4013d56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 2\\sqrt{2} \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"155\" height=\"30\" />.\n~jamespudi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B\">2007 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017144946\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 297/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7309/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.637      1 -total\n 60.80%    7.684      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.25%    4.834      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9472:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017144946 and revision id 288150. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}